    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1194">

                <pb facs="1244" n="1232" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.6711/4–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Packer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-27T20:00:00+03:00">April 27, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 28—4:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>571. ReEmb’s 472, April 7. The Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="33"
                        xml:id="d1194-f1"/> informed me this morning that there has been as yet no
                    reaction <pb facs="1245" n="1233" xml:id="pg1233"/> from the Russian side to the
                    Turkish note to the Soviet Ambassador here concerning the proposed discussions
                    to revise the Turkish-Soviet treaty of friendship and neutrality. The Minister
                    stated that he did not expect any Soviet proposal until after Molotov’s return
                    from San Francisco.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Packer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1194-f1" n="33" xml:id="d1194-f1-content">
